{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — Request Private Appointment (Wireframe 03 §05).

  The wireframe and the mobile brief both place this directly beneath Add to Bag,
  but neither defines what it does. Until Aloha decides (a modal enquiry form, a
  dedicated page, or an email route) this links to whichever page exists, in
  order of preference, and says plainly when none is bound.

  Reuses `custom.inquire_to_order` rather than inventing a parallel flag
  (docs/data-model.md §1). When the flag is set on a product the label is
  unchanged — the flag is carried here so the Phase 2 enquiry route can switch
  on it without touching this markup.

  Usage (inside a main-product custom_liquid block):
    {% render 'ha-appointment', text: 'Request Private Appointment',
         handle: 'private-appointment' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign label = text | default: 'Request Private Appointment'

  assign appt_page = nil
  if handle != blank
    assign appt_page = pages[handle]
  endif
  if appt_page == blank
    assign appt_page = pages['private-appointment']
  endif
  if appt_page == blank
    assign appt_page = pages['contact']
  endif
-%}

<div class="ha-pdp__appointment">
  {%- if appt_page != blank -%}
    <a class="ha-link ha-identify" href="{{ appt_page.url }}">{{ label }}</a>
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="ha-link ha-link--inert ha-identify">{{ label }}</span>
    {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note',
      show: true,
      text: 'Placeholder — no appointment page bound yet; route pending Aloha'
    -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
